 " to ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"6ba26e66-4241-4fd6-a7bf-dd484984ef75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The interval is ",
 StyleBox["I(u, v) = {w : d(u, w) + d(w, v) = d(u, v)}", "TI"],
 ". It contains ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " and is the union of all shortest paths from ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", the support of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraSegment"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSegment", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["u", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "929c4bec-856a-4e33-bc10-f4dea2da81dd"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6abef1f7-9d7d-4d0d-a9c7-48ab7cc585b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the plane the interval is the straight segment. On the square grid it is \
the rectangle with corners ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ": with ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " steps along one axis and ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " along the other it has ",
 StyleBox["(a + 1)(b + 1)", "TI"],
 " vertices."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8411a727-dbb2-41c2-bda4-fd7a61683ad6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " in different components give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b43a592-6e41-4aed-b19a-be69997b7dea"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0b077710-6ce9-4d84-bf48-8541b7fa51e4"],

Cell["Corresponding notion in the classical axiom systems:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"64b7f6a3-1d4c-46f6-8948-092951745cd1"],

